{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"ef2c4ae8657bd31e","name":"card_event_second_chance","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/Breakthrough/events/card_event_second_chance","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"SECOND CHANCE","text":"Draw two random orders from your deck.","flavorText":"At the beginning of WWII the British were ill prepared in saving aircrews that were downed over sea and RAF relied on its coastal defense force to rescue the crewmen, which was an uncoordinated effort and not very efficient. Following the heavy losses of aircrew in the Battle of Britain, RAF established their own Air Sea Rescue Services and rescue operations became increasingly efficient throughout the remainder of WWII. Aircrews were trained in techniques that would help to maximize their chances of survival and supplied with survival equipment such as inflatable dinghies copied from the German Luftwaffe. The air-sea rescue squadrons of the RAF flew a variety of aircraft, usually those that had been rejected or withdrawn from front line service. Spitfires and Boulton Paul Defiants were used to look for downed aircrew and Avro Ansons to drop supplies. Supermarine Walrus and Supermarine Sea Otter amphibious aircraft were used to pick up aircrew from the water. ","faction":"Britain","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_second_chance","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_second_chance_title","SourceString":"SECOND CHANCE","LocalizedString":"SECOND CHANCE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_second_chance_text","SourceString":"Draw two random orders from your deck.","LocalizedString":"Draw two random orders from your deck."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_second_chance_history","SourceString":"At the beginning of WWII the British